@page "/privacy"
@layout MainLayout

<PageTitle>Privacy - Fellowship Analyzer</PageTitle>

<div class="privacy-page">
    <PageHeader Title="Privacy">
        <Subtitle>What this site records, and what it does not.</Subtitle>
    </PageHeader>

    <section class="privacy-body">
        <h2>No cookies, no analytics storage</h2>
        <p>
            This site sets no cookies. It stores nothing on your device for analytics, loads no
            third-party analytics or advertising script, and cannot follow you to any other site.
        </p>
        <p>
            Reports you open are cached in your browser so reopening one does not fetch it again,
            and your theme choice is stored the same way. Both stay on your device and are never
            sent anywhere. Clearing your browser storage removes them.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site records about usage</h2>
        <p>
            The first time a given report, player and dungeon is analysed, the server records two
            things: the hero and the dungeon name. That record contains no player name, no character
            id, no report code and no account details, and it is never linked to a visitor.
        </p>
        <p>
            The server also counts how often each of its endpoints is called, without recording
            anything about which report was asked for.
        </p>

        <h2>What Azure records</h2>
        <p>
            The site runs on Azure Static Web Apps and its request data goes to Azure Application
            Insights. That is a Microsoft service, and what it keeps is set by Azure rather than by
            this site.
        </p>
        <p>
            For every request, Azure derives an approximate location from your network address,
            keeps the city, region and country, and discards the address itself. It also keeps the
            full web address of the request. For a report request that web address includes the
            report code, the player id and the dungeon id, because they are what the request asks
            for. Records of a failure can include a report code for the same reason: a failure that
            names no report cannot be investigated.
        </p>
        <p>
            Application Insights keeps this data for 90 days and then deletes it.
        </p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>
            Open an issue on
            <a href="https://github.com/Seriousnes/FellowshipAnalyzer/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
